// Background rules. Start at 0 and use 5 lines, and each block is spaced
// apart on multiples of 10. First line is an index into the description
// message file, the next line is an index into the effect message file,
// and the third line is the list of race-gender combinations for which
// the background is legal. If third line is left empty, all combinations
// can use the background. Otherwise the three letter codes are:
//
//	HUF - human female
//	HUM - human male
//	DWF - dwarf female
//	DWM - dwarf male
//	ELF - elf female
//	ELM - elf male
//	HEF - half elf female
//	HEM - half elf male
//	GNF - gnome female
//	GNM - gnome male
//	HAF - halfling female
//	HAM - halfling male
//	HOF - half orc female
//	HOM - half orc male
//	HGF - half ogre female
//	HGM - half ogre male
//	NPC - any NPC can use this background, regardless of their race or gender
//	ANY - anyone can use this background (same as blank line, included for clarity)
//
// The fourth line is how much money the background gives the character,
// and the last line is a list of item prototype numbers separated by spaces. It
// should be left blank unless items are supplied by the background.

